<article class="env-lemma" id="093W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/093W">Lemma <span data-tag="093W">13.33.6</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Assume colimits over $\mathbf{N}$ exist and are exact. Then countable direct sums exists and are exact. Moreover, if $(A_ n, f_ n)$ is a system over $\mathbf{N}$, then there is a short exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to \bigoplus A_ n \to \bigoplus A_ n \to \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits A_ n \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> where the first map in degree $n$ is given by $1 - f_ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement follows from $\bigoplus A_ n = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits (A_1 \oplus \ldots \oplus A_ n)$. For the second, note that for each $n$ we have the short exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to A_1 \oplus \ldots \oplus A_{n - 1} \to A_1 \oplus \ldots \oplus A_ n \to A_ n \to 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the first map is given by the maps $1 - f_ i$ and the second map is the sum of the transition maps. Take the colimit to get the sequence of the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>